The major source of armor and weapons are the mines and both
castles.  The initial inventories of monsters overwhelm what can
be found in shops.  And death drops eventually overwhel shops
for random items.

Initial monster inventories are another reason to go ahead and
level up - Start encountering orcs and you start getting armor and
weapons from them.

AC from orcs and then from gnomes and dwarves and then elves
in the mines end up supplying AC that would be purchased b
protection racket players.

On the other hand, AC from armor from monsters has weight.
Protection purchased from priests has negative weight - It
reduces the gold you carry.

There is another way to get devine protection - prayer.  Altar
dancing can get artifacts or protection and other benefits
depending on how you do it.  The difference between purchased
protection and altar dancing protection is the number of points
possible.  Altar dancing is only limited to -127.



